TI  - Targeted alveo-pleural fistula endobronchial valve treatment using ventilation 
      scintigraphy.
PG  - e01146
LID - 10.1002/rcr2.1146 [doi]
LID - e01146
AB  - Persistent air-leaks can be difficult to localize in radiology. Bronchoscopic 
      management of air-leaks requires identification of the leak's location to allow 
      suitable targeted treatment. One-way endobronchial valves have become a suitable 
      option for persistent air-leaks. In this report, a combination scintigraphy and 
      one-way endobronchial valve treatment successfully resolved a persistent 
      air-leak.
