TI  - Enhancing antifungal treatment for chronic cavitary pulmonary aspergillosis 
      through the addition of endobronchial valve therapy.
PG  - 102106
LID - 10.1016/j.rmcr.2024.102106 [doi]
LID - 102106
AB  - A 62-year-old male experienced anti-MDA5 dermatomyositis with lung involvement, 
      treated with immunosuppressive therapy leading to chronic cavitary pulmonary 
      aspergillosis in left upper lobe. Patient's history was complicated by complete 
      left pneumothorax due to alveolar-pleural fistula occurring because of the 
      rupture of the pulmonary cavitation. Left lung failed to re-expand despite a 
      four-week period of pleural drainage. In addition to antifungal therapy, patient 
      received endobronchial valve therapy in the anterior segmental bronchus of the 
      left upper lobe leading to air leak cessation, left lung re expansion and 
      aspergillosis cavitation closure.
