TI  - LigaSure meets endobronchial valve in a case of lung cancer with pneumoconiosis.
PG  - 308-10
LID - 10.3978/j.issn.2218-6751.2012.12.09 [doi]
AB  - Resection of lung cancer associated with pneumoconiosis may be difficult since 
      fibrosis limits the exposure of hilum, and the use of stapler; yet, surgery may 
      be complicated by persistent air leaks due to the underlying disease. In this 
      setting, LigaSure was used to perform the tumor resection, and the postoperative 
      treatment of air leaks in the same patient was treated with placement of 
      endobronchial valves.
